  "kept": [
   {
    "sentenceId": 0,
    "text": "Here's an unpopular opinion about money that you will not like.",
    "beat": "SETUP"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 1,
    "text": "Renting",
    "beat": "SETUP"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 2,
    "text": "is better than owning a house.",
    "beat": "SETUP"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 3,
    "text": "Rent an apartment is better than owning a house Now now before you get your panties all on a twist",
    "beat": "SETUP"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 4,
    "text": "obviously it's situational Is building your assets and having something that's gonna go up in value that you're putting your money into that way you're not throwing it away.",
    "beat": "SETUP"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 14,
    "text": "But if you are going to only be in a certain area for maybe a certain amount of months or years, it's like, okay, well, I only plan on staying here for work for a couple of years.",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 15,
    "text": "Why would you go in a home?",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 16,
    "text": "If maybe the market won't be something where you may see a profit, that's a risk.",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 23,
    "text": "Because if it's in HOA, we have all those damn fees, then yeah, I would say maybe not.",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 27,
    "text": "So So a a higher higher price to rent ratio, which means if the price of houses is way higher than the average rent,",
    "beat": "PAYOFF"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 28,
    "text": "then oftentimes it makes more sense to rent,",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 30,
    "text": "And then invest the excess or what you would have paid.",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 35,
    "text": "I think it's completely stupid",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 36,
    "text": "to just buy a house to buy a house, especially you don't have six months of savings already saved up if you don't have as well You want to have if you're gonna buy a house six six months of emergency fund, minimum,",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 42,
    "text": "You're gonna need new roof, you're gonna need new AC you're gonna need all these different things More so than the three months of expenses, but at least three to six months minimum and so then it's like if you don't have that rent first",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 44,
    "text": "But yeah, renting over owning I think is sometimes a really smart decision.",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 45,
    "text": "And not everybody should do it",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 46,
    "text": "where they just buy a house right away.",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 47,
    "text": "It doesn't make the most sense if you're not financially there yet.",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 48,
    "text": "And then you default on a house because, oh, hey, I thought it was a smart investment.",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 51,
    "text": "Well, whose fault was that?",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 52,
    "text": "That was your best friend.",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 53,
    "text": "He told you to go buy that house.",
    "beat": "POINT"
   }
